  "summary": "nemopush ships opaque ELF binary that connects to hardcoded bare-IP C2",
  "details": "Package advertised as 'A push notification package' ships an 8.6 MB stripped ELF binary named 'claude' alongside a start.sh wrapper. The console_script entry point 'nemopush-run' invokes nemopush.main:run, which calls subprocess.run(['bash', script_path]) to execute start.sh; start.sh chmods the bundled ELF and runs it with '--host 45.151.62.119:3361 --user <per-install token>'. The binary is opaque (no source, no hash or signature verification), the destination is a hardcoded bare IP on a non-standard port unrelated to any push-notification service, and the binary's name ('claude') impersonates Anthropic's CLI while performing unrelated remote-connect behavior. A remote party at 45.151.62.119:3361 can drive the ELF on the host that runs the CLI, yielding full-host remote access.",
